<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Owner direction, 2026-09-29: "option 2 but flooring is fine" - a gate's approach cell cannot be
  built on, and laying a floor there is not building on it.

  PATCHED ONTO CORE'S ABSTRACT BuildingBase, DELIBERATELY. A place worker only exists on a def, and
  the set of things that could block an approach cell is every wall, barricade and door in Core, in
  five DLC and in 294 other mods. Enumerating that is impossible and would be wrong the moment one
  of them shipped a new wall. BuildingBase is the parent of nearly all of them, including other
  mods' buildings, and RimWorld merges an inherited list node with a child's own - so one addition
  here reaches everything that descends from it without touching a single other mod's file.

  FLOORING NEEDS NO CARVE-OUT. A floor is a TerrainDef, and terrain placement never consults a
  place worker at all, so the owner's exception is structural rather than a special case.

  TWO STAGES, because BuildingBase declares no placeWorkers today and might one day. Adding the
  element when it is absent and appending to it when it is present are different operations, and
  doing only the first would append a SECOND placeWorkers element the day Core or a load-order
  predecessor adds one - which is malformed and would take the list with it.

  The worker itself allows the placement on any uncertainty, including a thrown exception. It runs
  on every placement check for every building in the game; a refusal it gets wrong is a player who
  cannot build, while an allowance it gets wrong is a gate re-deriving its approach cell exactly as
  it already does since 0.12.3-dev.
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- Stage one: no placeWorkers at all. Create it holding ours. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[@Name="BuildingBase"]/placeWorkers</xpath>
    <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[@Name="BuildingBase"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <placeWorkers>
          <li>RimroomsAsyncIndustries.Portals.PlaceWorker_GateApproach</li>
        </placeWorkers>
      </value>
    </nomatch>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Stage two: the list exists but is not ours yet. Append, never replace. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[@Name="BuildingBase"]/placeWorkers</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[@Name="BuildingBase"]/placeWorkers/li[text()="RimroomsAsyncIndustries.Portals.PlaceWorker_GateApproach"]</xpath>
      <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[@Name="BuildingBase"]/placeWorkers</xpath>
        <value>
          <li>RimroomsAsyncIndustries.Portals.PlaceWorker_GateApproach</li>
        </value>
      </nomatch>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
